    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The helper’s sync path changed from returning the downstream refresh result to returning the raw `fetch()` response. `GoogleCalendarService.refreshAccessToken` immediately dereferences `res?.data`, and the same helper is used by other changed services that expect to deserialize a token response after awaiting the helper. With the new implementation, a caller that takes the sync branch gets a `Response` instance, not the token JSON object it previously received, so `res.data`/token-field reads will be undefined unless the caller performs an extra parse step. Also observed in: packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/refreshOAuthTokens.ts",
